{
  "_comment": [
    "Single source of truth for the timezone picker.",
    "",
    "Each entry maps a human label to a POSIX TZ rule. The rule, not a plain",
    "offset, is what the firmware stores - it carries the daylight-saving",
    "changeover dates, so the clock corrects itself twice a year on its own.",
    "",
    "POSIX offsets are WEST-positive, the opposite sign to the 'UTC+05:30' that",
    "people write. Asia/Kolkata at UTC+05:30 is therefore 'IST-5:30'. Getting",
    "this backwards is the classic bug here.",
    "",
    "After editing, run:  python tools/gen_timezones.py",
    "which regenerates the picker inside firmware/src/web_ui.h. CI fails if the",
    "two drift apart."
  ],
